   "evidence": "`grep -rn 'import (PhyslibAlpha|Physlib)\\.QuantumMechanics' upstream/Physlib/PhyslibAlpha/Relativity` returns no matches: no PhyslibAlpha `Relativity` module depends on `QuantumMechanics`, so this file cannot move upstream whole at its mirrored path. `structure AngularMomentumRepresentation` is at `upstream/Physlib/PhyslibAlpha/QuantumMechanics/AngularMomentum/Basic.lean:59`; the proofs of `toEuclideanLin_pauliMatrix_mul_self` (lines 76-79) and `sum_tensorProductMap_toEuclideanLin_pauliMatrix_inr` (lines 156-186) use only `Physlib...PauliMatrices.Basic`, `PhyslibAlpha...PauliMatrices.SelfAdjoint` and Mathlib.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/PauliMatrices/BasicExtensions.lean",
   "fix": "Split: keep `toEuclideanLin_pauliMatrix_mul_self` and `sum_tensorProductMap_toEuclideanLin_pauliMatrix_inr` in `Relativity/PauliMatrices/BasicExtensions.lean` (dropping the `SpinOrbit` import), and move the spin-representation declarations listed above to a module at the PhyslibAlpha path they would occupy, e.g. `EpsilonEridani/QuantumMechanics/AngularMomentum/SpinHalf.lean`, imported by `SpinDecomposition.lean`.",
   "issue": "The module is declared as the mirror of `Physlib.Relativity.PauliMatrices.Basic` (first import, mirrored path), but half its content \u2014 `spinGen`, `spinGen_apply`, `sum_spinGen_mul_self`, `lie_spinGen_zero_one/one_two/two_zero`, `spinRep`, `spinRep_Jx/Jy/Jz`, `Jsq_spinRep`, `dot_spinRep_spinRep` \u2014 is quantum-mechanics angular-momentum material whose home structure `PhyslibAlpha.Sl2.AngularMomentumRepresentation` is defined in `PhyslibAlpha/QuantumMechanics/AngularMomentum/Basic.lean`. It forces `public import PhyslibAlpha.QuantumMechanics.AngularMomentum.SpinOrbit` on the Pauli-basics module, so the two declarations that depend on no angular-momentum theory (`toEuclideanLin_pauliMatrix_mul_self`, `sum_tensorProductMap_toEuclideanLin_pauliMatrix_inr`) cannot be used, or contributed upstream, without the whole angular-momentum stack.",
   "line": 10
  }
